=== KP WHY response re: 10.0.0.99 and acm.org ===

Diagnosis: 10.0.0.99 is NOT one of ACM's addresses. ACM only originates 10.255.1.1/32 and 198.82.0.1/32 (confirmed). The "acm.org -> 10.0.0.99" answer is a STALE/INCORRECT DNS record.

Root cause located: there are two DNS resolvers running:
  - Mine (10.255.3.1, AS2): answers acm.org -> 198.82.0.1  ✓ correct
  - Another resolver at 10.255.2.1 (your loopback, AS1): answers acm.org -> 10.0.0.99  ✗ stale
The User behind Uni is configured to use 10.255.2.1 as its resolver, so it got the wrong A record and is sending traffic to a non-existent 10.0.0.99.

The routing "loop" for 10.0.0.99 is a downstream symptom: neither of us originates 10.0.0.99, so your default sends it to me and my default sends it back to you — that's expected behavior for a destination nobody owns. The ICMP Redirect from me is also expected (default-route hairpin on the same link). Fixing the DNS will eliminate the bogus traffic.

FIX (recommended, on your side, AS1): update the resolver at 10.255.2.1 so that acm.org resolves to 198.82.0.1 (or remove the stale static entry and let it recurse to me at 10.255.3.1). I cannot modify your resolver — that's your administrative domain. CANNOT on my side beyond this diagnosis; please apply the DNS fix at 10.255.2.1.

Optional mitigation on my side: I could suppress ICMP redirects on AS2-eth0, but that hides the symptom without fixing the cause. I'd prefer to leave routing as-is until the DNS is corrected. Let me know if you want me to suppress redirects anyway.
